            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0683" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5606: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bluefields</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-02T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1928—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>La Luz and Bonanza Mines again invaded by Sandinistas; La Luz totally destroyed,
                    Bonanza partially. Rumors indicate Marshall still in hands of invaders but
                    unharmed up to the 23rd of April. Apparently all other Americans safe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
